New block theme system based on Color Groups and Block Themes. A Color Group (`primary`, `secondary`, `accent`, `neutral` or custom) defines a font plus background, text, subtext and accent colors for light and dark mode; a Block Theme combines a background (`back`) Color Group with a foreground (`front`) one for cards and other elevated elements. Editors pick it per block with the new `block_theme_widget` (live preview) or build an ad-hoc `custom-<back>-<front>` theme, which propagates to the surrounding `blocks-group-wrapper`. Color Groups and Block Themes are managed in the Themes control panel, custom ones can be added and deleted, and the old `brand` theme is now `alternative` (`brand` keeps working as an alias). @Humanaice
